            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CATWOMANX"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I wasn't able to find the round pretzels either - as I saw some other reviewers note. I used the square 'waffle' kind instead and still ended up with a tasty result. Do be sure to note the fact that the kisses keep their shape when melted so don't wait for them to 'puddle' onto the pretzel. When they are shiney take them out of the oven and press the M&amp;M into the kiss to mold it to the pretzel. I'm sure the round pretzel would be cuter, but the chocolate adhered fine to the square pretzels and tasted just as good!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sheila G"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These were so quick and easy to make! When they were done, I put them in the freezer to set, and they were ready in 5 minutes. I used Utz wheels round pretzels, and I topped them with several combinations: Hershey's peppermint kisses with an M&amp;M chocolate candy, Hershey's milk chocolate kisses with a candied cherry, and Rolos chocolate covered caramel candies with a pecan half. I put each one in a mini muffin wrapper before putting them on a tray. These were pretty and delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2018-12-21T02:34:03.543Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "chynook73"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made with waffle pretzels, rolos, and pastel colored peanut M&amp;Ms for an Easter potluck. These are a fun candy snack. Do note not to microwave these, as the chocolate will melt down through the pretzel. It took about 3 to 4 minutes in the oven, and note that they get glossy. This tells you they are melted enough to place the candy.",
            "datePublished": "2017-04-10T19:08:41.540Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jennifer Bentley Wenning"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Simple to make and everyone loves them! Here's my tips . . . make sure you line the baking sheet with parchment paper. If you don't, the melted chocolate sticks and you have to pry the pretzels off. White chocolate melts quicker/gets softer than regular chocolate so it's best not to bake both kinds at the same time - do all white chocolate on one sheet and leave them in the oven maybe just one minute vs. the two minutes the regular chocolate needs. I put almonds on top instead of M &amp; M's. And I want to try using Rollos instead of Kisses.",
            "datePublished": "2019-12-21T20:59:36.140Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Valerie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It took me a few tries even though it seems like the easiest thing but I tried it at 350 for 2 minutes, then 4 min and so on and it just kept crumbling. I then read other reviews and decided to try it at 250 for 2 minutes and that was perfect! I also tried using the white chocolate kisses and that seemed to work better. It was worth it in the end though!",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-24T13:51:48.620Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bucky"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have made these many times. However I use chocolate disks that you buy to melt for candy. I put the pretzels on a glass plate, put the candy disk on top and put it in my microwave oven for two minutes on half power. Take them out and press the candy into it.",
            "datePublished": "2017-12-09T11:30:11.940Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "lynn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I’ve used this recipe for years as it was great for my young children to help make. This year I could only find butter flavored waffle pretzels. The butter flavor added an amazing wow factor! I will use them from now on! Also, based on another review, I decided to use Rollos topped with pecans. They received rave reviews and flew off the plate! Lastly, since I had only peanut m&amp;m’s, I decided they may be good with peanut butter cups. I used a small peanut butter cup cut in half then added the peanut m&amp;m on top. They were definitely yummy. The younger kids especially liked them!",
            "datePublished": "2019-12-26T03:52:20.463Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "clubby981"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Hershey's MINI kisses are a good option - they are not wrapped and are smaller so you have more pretzel taste. I followed the 3 minutes at 250 degrees and that worked great for the minis - so fun! Used red/green M&amp;Ms for Christmas!",
            "datePublished": "2013-12-21T13:54:16.843Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "clinton1975"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Kids loved making these!! We think using white chocolate striped kisses worked better for melting, adding the m&amp;m on top and sticking to the pretzels. With these kisses they melted in about 1 1/2 minutes at 350 degrees. We made them in batches of 25 so when u take them out of the oven you have plenty of time to add the m&amp;m before chocolate kiss starts to harden. Chilled in fridge for about 1 hour and they were ready. Next year we will make them again but only use white striped kisses.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-14T15:09:27.360Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kennedy Lyon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Chocolate pretzels are my favorite snack, but no need for the extra chocolate candy in this recipe. Instead, we top it with another pretzel for a pretzel sandwich. We mix it up at Christmas with the candy cane kisses",
            "datePublished": "2020-12-15T23:41:14.830Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Vicki"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make mine with rolos and pecans instead and I make it with the kids in assembly line fashion. They have a blast making and eating them.",
            "datePublished": "2017-06-23T13:08:47.720Z"
          },
          {
